  (text "2.4 GHz RF RECEIVER FRONT-END - SCHEMATIC DRAFT (rev A)\nNet names, references and pin numbers match 2G4_RF_Receiver_FrontEnd.kicad_pcb (cross-checked by script).\nERC has not been run in KiCad.\n\nOPEN ITEMS (details in LAYOUT_NOTES.md)\n1. L1 is drawn in series after C1. Confirm the input match topology against the MAX2644 datasheet Fig. 1 / Fig. 2.\n2. C3: Fig. 1 (high gain) uses 2.2 pF. Fig. 2 (high linearity) uses 15 pF and adds L2 = 3.9 nH, which is not placed here.\n   The BOM lists C3 = 15 pF and no L2.\n3. Datasheet VCC bypass spacing from U1: C3 0.041 in, C2 0.352 in, supply line 0.532 in x 0.012 in (layout constraint).\n4. FL1 insertion loss (1.5 dB typ / 1.7 dB max) sits ahead of the LNA and adds to system noise figure.\n5. R1 sets bias current. Leaving BIAS open puts the LNA in standby.\n6. RF lines are 50 ohm grounded coplanar waveguide on RO4003C 0.813 mm (W 1.6 mm, gap 0.3 mm)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 134.62 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "97b90304-7611-5628-a123-523e15bbd325"))
